      "key": "fed.fica.wage_definition.exclusions",
      "value": "FICA wages (IRC 3121(a)) are all remuneration for employment, including non-cash remuneration, except among others: (a)(1) pay above the OASDI wage base (OASDI only); (a)(2) sickness, accident, medical and hospitalization plan payments; (a)(5) payments to or from qualified plans (401(a), 403(a), SEP, 403(b) other than salary reduction, governmental 457, SIMPLE other than elective contributions) and (5)(G) section 125 cafeteria-plan benefits that would not be wages outside the plan; (a)(12) non-cash tips and cash tips under 20 a month; (a)(18) 127/129/134 benefits; (a)(19) meals and lodging excludable under 119; (a)(20) 74(c), 108(f)(4), 117 and 132 fringes. 3121(v)(1): 401(k) elective deferrals and 414(h) salary-reduction pickups remain FICA wages.",
